Yes: nothing in it is written down ahead of time. The server makes the This server section each time the link is read. It takes the address from the request itself, the host and port the session used to reach it, so it is right wherever the server runs.

Wording I will apply:

> - the API's address, made from the address the session reached the server at (`http://<host>:<port>/api`);
